do $seed$
declare cid uuid;
begin
  select id into cid from public.courses where slug = 'bib-102';
  insert into public.course_items (course_id, kind, position, title, content) select cid, 'topic', 3, $j$1.3 The Miracles and Parables of Jesus$j$, $j${"readings": [{"title": "Mark 4 (King James Version)", "url": "/portal/bible/Mark/4"}, {"title": "Mark 5 (King James Version)", "url": "/portal/bible/Mark/5"}, {"title": "Luke 15 (King James Version)", "url": "/portal/bible/Luke/15"}, {"title": "John 11 (King James Version)", "url": "/portal/bible/John/11"}], "body": "Read Mark 4, Mark 5, Luke 15 and John 11 in the King James Version. Then read this lesson.\n\nJesus taught with words and with power. His miracles showed that He had authority over sickness, nature, evil spirits and even death. He calmed a storm with a word, healed the sick, cast out demons and raised the dead, including Lazarus, whom He called from the tomb. He also taught in parables, which are short stories that use daily life to show a spiritual truth. In the parable of the prodigal son a father welcomes home a son who wasted everything, and it shows the love of God for sinners who come home.\n\nKey words: miracle, authority, parable, compassion, resurrection.\n\nYour task: (1) Tell what Jesus said to the wind and the sea. (2) Explain what a parable is and why Jesus used them. (3) Tell what the father did when he saw his son coming home (Luke 15:20).\n\nCourse area: Bible elective. Scripture is read from the King James Version.", "video": "", "presenter": "Dr. Alex L. Jenkins Sr.", "standards": "Bible elective", "script": "So far we have seen the birth of Jesus, His baptism and His teaching. Now we look at the two ways He showed who He was, through miracles and through parables.\n\nA miracle is an act of God's power that goes beyond what nature can do. Jesus did not perform miracles to entertain people. Each one showed that He had authority and that the kingdom of God had come. In Mark 4 Jesus and His disciples were crossing the Sea of Galilee when a great storm arose. Jesus was asleep in the boat, and the disciples woke Him in fear. He stood up, rebuked the wind and said in Mark 4:39, Peace, be still. And the wind ceased, and there was a great calm. The disciples marveled and asked, What manner of man is this, that even the wind and the sea obey him?\n\nIn Mark 5 He healed a woman who had been sick for twelve years and raised a girl from the dead. In John 11 He came to the tomb of His friend Lazarus, who had been dead four days. Jesus told Martha in John 11:25, I am the resurrection, and the life: he that believeth in me, though he were dead, yet shall he live. Then He called Lazarus out of the tomb, and he came out alive.\n\nJesus also taught in parables. A parable is a short story from everyday life that carries a spiritual truth. People who were ready to listen understood, and people who were not ready had to think about it. The most loved of the parables is the one about the prodigal son in Luke 15. A younger son took his inheritance, left home and wasted it all. When he came to himself, he decided to go home. Luke 15:20 says, But when he was yet a great way off, his father saw him, and had compassion, and ran, and fell on his neck, and kissed him. That is a picture of how God receives every sinner who returns.\n\nYour task is to tell what Jesus said to the wind, explain what a parable is, and tell what the father did. Then take the four question check.\n\nHe has power over every storm, and He welcomes every son and daughter home. Excellence, Faith, Purpose. I will see you in the next lesson."}$j$::jsonb where not exists (select 1 from public.course_items where course_id = cid and kind = 'topic' and title = $j$1.3 The Miracles and Parables of Jesus$j$);
end
$seed$;
